1
00:00:00,275 --> 00:00:01,775
(Sheldon:)- It was a drizzly Tuesday.
- Okay.

2
00:00:03,237 --> 00:00:05,237
(Penny:)You promised me
you would keep my secret...

3
00:00:05,406 --> 00:00:08,116
...so you are just gonna have to
figure out a way to do it.

4
00:00:09,284 --> 00:00:11,664
(Sheldon(entering):)Leonard, I'm moving out.

5
00:00:14,707 --> 00:00:16,997
(Leonard:)What do you mean
you're moving out? Why?

6
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:19,627
(Sheldon:)There doesn't have to be a reason.

7
00:00:20,921 --> 00:00:23,841
- Yeah, there kind of does.
- Not necessarily.

8
00:00:24,007 --> 00:00:26,887
(Sheldon:)This is a classic example
of Münchausen's trilemma.

9
00:00:27,052 --> 00:00:31,012
(Sheldon:)Either the reason is predicated on a series
of sub-reasons leading to regression...

10
00:00:31,181 --> 00:00:34,811
...or it tracks back to axiomatic statements,
or it's ultimately circular...

11
00:00:34,977 --> 00:00:38,147
...i. e., I'm moving out
because I'm moving out.

12
00:00:40,232 --> 00:00:41,442
(Leonard:)I'm still confused.

13
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:44,698
(Sheldon:)Leonard, I don't see
how I could've made it any simpler.

14
00:00:45,696 --> 00:00:48,366
Hey, qu'est-ce que c'up?

15
00:00:49,408 --> 00:00:52,408
(Raj:)We just got back from that exhibit
of those plasticized cadavers.

16
00:00:52,578 --> 00:00:55,708
(Howard:)Some of those skinless chicks were hot.

17
00:00:56,707 --> 00:01:00,027
(Sheldon:)If you'll excuse me, I'm going to pack.

